# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extension C — service isolation for BACKEND B
# Lives on: Dikshant's laptop (Mac 4, 10.7.24.165), protecting port 3002
# Install to: /etc/pf.anchors/admv
#
# Same shape as Backend A's anchor. See pf-backend-a.anchor for why the pass
# rules precede the block and why "block drop" produces a timeout.
#
# This laptop also hosts the standby edge; when the standby is active it reaches
# this backend over 127.0.0.1 (loopback), which never traverses en0 and so is
# not affected by these rules.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- allow the PRIMARY edge (Mukul, Mac 2) --
pass in quick on en0 proto tcp from 10.7.25.158 to any port 3002

# -- refuse everyone else ---------------------------------------------------
block drop in quick on en0 proto tcp to any port 3002
